      "number": 48,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Use backtracking (DFS). Iterate through each cell of the board. If a cell matches the first letter of the word, start a DFS from that cell. In the DFS, explore adjacent cells (up, down, left, right) if they match the next character in the word and haven't been visited in the current path. Mark visited cells to avoid cycles within a single search path.\nTime complexity: O(N * M * 4^L) where N*M is board size, L is word length. Space complexity: O(L) for recursion stack or O(N*M) for visited set (if not modifying board)\nAlgorithms: Backtracking, Depth-First Search (DFS)\nData Structures: 2D Array (Board), Set (or modify board for visited status)\nKey concepts: Grid traversal, Path finding, Recursive exploration, Pruning search space",
