      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/remove-duplicates-from-sorted-array-ii\" target=\"_blank\">80. Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array II</a>",
      "number": 49,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Use a two-pointer approach (read and write pointer). Iterate through the array with the read pointer. If the current element is different from the element at write_pointer - 2 (or if write_pointer &lt; 2), it means we can include this element (as it's either a new number or the second occurrence of the current number). Place it at write_pointer and increment write_pointer.\nTime complexity: O(n), Space complexity: O(1)\nAlgorithms: Two Pointers, Array Manipulation\nData Structures: Array\nKey concepts: In-place modification, Duplicate handling with count limit, Sorted array properties",
