      "explanation": "Use a modified binary search. The main challenge is handling duplicates, which can make it O(n) in worst case (e.g., [1,1,1,1,0,1,1]). If nums[mid] == nums[low] == nums[high], you can't determine which half is sorted, so increment low and decrement high to shrink the search space. Otherwise, logic is similar to non-duplicate version: check which half is sorted and if target lies there.\nTime complexity: O(log n) on average, O(n) in worst case. Space complexity: O(1).\nAlgorithms: Binary Search (modified)\nData Structures: Array\nKey concepts: Rotated array with duplicates, Ambiguity in sorted half, Worst-case linear scan",
